{"id": "tea:mahavairocana-sutra:1", "source": "src:mahavairocana-sutra", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "The Lord teaches that the gnosis of omniscience has bodhicitta as its cause, compassion as its root and skilful means as its culmination.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-phrases-mahavairocana"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U44-indian-vajrayana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; not located in a local text. The 'three phrases' of ch. 1.", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U44-indian-vajrayana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:mahavairocana-sutra:1.mind", "source": "src:mahavairocana-sutra", "location": {"ref": "1.mind"}, "paraphrase": "What is awakening? It is to know one's own mind as it truly is.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-phrases-mahavairocana"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U44-indian-vajrayana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; not located in a local text.", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U44-indian-vajrayana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:mahavairocana-sutra:2", "source": "src:mahavairocana-sutra", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "The Womb maṇḍala arisen from great compassion is taught, with the Buddha Mahāvairocana at the centre of an eight-petalled lotus and the families in enclosures around.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:womb-and-vajra-mandalas"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U44-indian-vajrayana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; not located in a local text.", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U44-indian-vajrayana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:mahavairocana-sutra:a-syllable", "source": "src:mahavairocana-sutra", "location": {"ref": "a-syllable"}, "paraphrase": "The letter A is the gate of all dharmas because they are originally unborn; meditation on the letters, above all A, is taught as the way of mantra.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:syllable-a"], "practices": ["prc:a-syllable-meditation"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U44-indian-vajrayana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; not located in a local text. The same formula is quoted from the Hevajra in the local Amanasikārādhāra.", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U44-indian-vajrayana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
